# WHAT IT COVERS: the 2026-11-11 stream, 74.0 minutes cut to the gameplay its video shows,
# captured through Windows.Graphics.Capture with o:vsync on 92e3e29, and the first capture made
# with the step tolerance on (-steptol 18: 3000 us, easing back 500 us a present). It carries
# step_tolerance_pct 18, so every arm of the replay runs the rule as the relay did; a change
# that alters what the rule decides shows here against the field's own numbers, where the
# other fixtures only compare two replays. The game hitched (20 to 100 ms) 99 times (80 an
# hour) and stalled for 100 ms or more 27 times (22 an hour), in 28 bursts, 19 of them with a
# stall; the longest stalls are 518 ms at about 640 s and 481 ms at about 4150 s. No periodic
# stretch. A calm stream for the rule: 20 of its 4438 seconds had uneven source frame times
# and none ran 3 s. The worst blend run is 25 presents in the field and the replay.
# WINDOW. The video pairs with this log at log time = video time + 42.470 s, from the 2886
# marked frames in its first 48 s, 2883 of them on time within 0.42 ms of that offset (p90).
# The video runs 4437.6 s with no holes; it opens and ends on gameplay, so the cut is its
# whole span, 42.5 s to 4480.0 s. Inside the cut, 8 seconds in 8 runs fall out of the 60 fps
# regime, each a single hitch second. About 20 minutes of it (video 35 to 55 min) hold
# cutscenes the game plays at 30 pictures a second on 60 new frames; the relay passes every
# frame there and the policy sees an ordinary 60 fps source.
# FIDELITY. The capture ran the policy the tree ships, with the rule at the setting the key
# names, so the two lines are comparable. The replay line (the plain arm, no dejitter) reads
# synth 0.4% against 0.4%, worst run 25 against 25, runs >= 50 0 against 0 and pull wraps 47
# against 47. On the dejitter arm, which is how the stream ran, the worst run is 25 as well.
# Counted over the window, replay against field: synthesized presents 1003 against 1008, repeats
# 131 against 128, skips 62 against 62, pull wraps 47 against 47. The lock released 5 times in
# the field and 5 on the replay, each pair within 0.48 ms. The replay makes 30 moves, 8 of them
# late, and 4 land more than 2 ms from a real frame. With the rule off the same replay
# synthesizes 598 an hour with the same worst run, and its content step is less even: rms over
# every step 475 us against 456 as run, steps off by over 2 ms 0.31% against 0.22%.
# Bounds on the REPLAY (not the field): inequalities, so an improvement passes and only a
# regression fails. Measured on the policy the capture ran.
max_worst_run 25
max_long_runs 0
max_synth_pct 0.8
min_reseeds 29
max_pull_wraps 47
